        "original_id": "6bd2eb6b-a980-58ae-929e-de0f5743844a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Rickman, Sissy Spacek, Loretta Lynn, Tommy Lee Jones, Martha Plimpton, Beverly D'Angelo, Patsy Cline, Stella Kowalski\n- Works: Coal Miner's Daughter, Hooper, Tuesdays with Morrie, Truman, The River Rat, A Streetcar Named Desire\n- Roles: film director, screenwriter, actress\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Actress, Golden Globe Award, Emmy Award\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Rickman, sometimes credited as Tom Rickman, is an American film director and screenwriter known for Coal Miner's Daughter, Hooper, Tuesdays with Morrie, and Truman.\n- Coal Miner's Daughter stars Sissy Spacek as Loretta Lynn, and that role earned Sissy Spacek the Academy Award for Best Actress.\n- Beverly D'Angelo was nominated for a Golden Globe Award for playing Patsy Cline in Coal Miner's Daughter (1980).\n- The River Rat is a 1984 independent family film directed by Thomas Rickman and starring Tommy Lee Jones and Martha Plimpton.\n- Beverly D'Angelo has appeared in more than 60 films.\n- Beverly D'Angelo was nominated for an Emmy Award for playing Stella Kowalski in the 1984 TV film A Streetcar Named Desire.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
